; This scenario was created by Adam Luker
; (zot@aapc.com), in the hopes that it might 
; be enjoyed.

BEGINTEXT
                              

                              ***** Vhalsecc *****

               The Second Empire did not collapse so much as it
       calcified. Worlds that had grown dependent on Imperial
       infrastructure found themselves stranded, forced to maintain
       what they could with dwindling resources. Innovation became
       dangerous. Expansion became threatening. And the province of
       Vhalsecc -- vast, wealthy, and ruled by twin magistrates who
       could not agree on anything except their own supremacy --
       became the enforcer of stagnation.

NEWPAGE                
                              
                              ***** Vhalsecc *****   

               "Vhalsecc held itself apart from the decay. Its worlds
       remained productive, its fleets remained strong, and its
       magistrates remained vigilant. Any attempt by neighboring systems
       to rebuild was met with swift punishment. Vhalsecc would not
       tolerate rivals. The galaxy, in Vhalsecc's view, belonged to
       Vhalsecc -- and would remain so until the stars themselves
       burned out."
                                        
                                        - History of the Galaxy
                                          Zex Narphil, Counselor
        
NEWPAGE
                              
                              ***** Vhalsecc *****    

               Your empire is small, crowded, and restless. Your people
       look to the stars and see opportunity. Your throne looks to the
       stars and sees danger. Vhalsecc watches, and Vhalsecc does not
       forgive.

               But you cannot hold your people back forever. Expand,
       or be consumed by your own unrest. Build your fleet, break the
       Vhalseccan grip, and forge something new from the wreckage of
       the old order.

               They are already watching you. Make sure they have
       reason to be afraid.

NEWPAGE

ENDTEXT

; --- World flavor text ---

BEGINDESCRIPTION

WorldBackgroundIndex
2:1 E:0          1 ; Player 1 Capital
2:3 E:1          1 ; Player 2 Capital
2:5 E:2          1 ; Player 3 Capital
2:6 E:3          1 ; Player 4 Capital
2:8 E:4          2 ; Vhalsecc 1 (empire 5)
2:12 E:5         2 ; Vhalsecc 2 (empire 6)
2:16 E:6         3 ; Empire 7, the pirates
2:17 E:7         4 ; Empire 8, the berzerker empire
3:1 E:7          5 ; Rogue Starbase
EndIndex

TEXT 1
Only by defeating Vhalsecc will you be able to expand your empire.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 2
One of the Vhalseccan capitals, this is one of your primary targets
ENDTEXT

TEXT 3
This is the capital of the pirate empire.  An effecient 
jumpbase, it would be a strong asset under your flag.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 4
This world controls the Starbase that roams these sectors. 
Conquering this planet would most effectively stop the 
starbase from tormenting you.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 5
This starbase poses a great threat to your systems.  By 
disabling the planet that controls it, you can stop it
from ravaging your worlds.  That won't be so easy, though.
ENDTEXT

ENDDESCRIPTION

